Body:
Skill-based workaround: add `variants` to `opencode.jsonc` for the provider's `glm-5.2` entry, sourced from `models.dev` `reasoning_options`. Example for `ollama-cloud`:

```jsonc
"provider": {
  "ollama-cloud": {
    "models": {
      "glm-5.2": {
        "variants": {
          "high": { "reasoningEffort": "high" },
          "max": { "reasoningEffort": "max" }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Config variants are merged after the generated ones, so this exposes `high`/`max` in the model selector today without waiting on core `reasoning_options` support. Restart opencode to load it.
